<p>European Union envoys on April 22 gave preliminary approval to a €90 billion loan package for Ukraine after months of delay, and formal sign-off by the 27 member states is expected to follow quickly. The breakthrough came after Ukraine said it had finished repairs and restarted the Druzhba pipeline segment that carries Russian oil through Ukraine to Hungary and Slovakia, ending a stoppage that had lasted since late January. The deal reflects a difficult wartime trade-off. Kyiv gets badly needed financing for military and financial support in 2026-2027, while Hungary and Slovakia regain access to crude supplies they had demanded before dropping their objections. The move also broke an intra-EU deadlock as the war stretches beyond four years, and several outlets said EU diplomats also advanced a new sanctions package against Russia alongside the loan decision.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/K7K_KC_KEIOVbystwYy55T7RNb_Bqm4exnmMFKvyjqK_o85SZTVYRS5bGJ2aSnNgb9qKrqEFQeND5HZ4RiHYDb3reWJ3_kVLSck6Nrm6_QcdHlmPAMX2P4QHNKlm_gy-IGUUli98TUXx3YewEVbz-H1dBk9f25yPYnU1Ek8BkGjs729Cx0axUN_z-Ww_WTxfqa_wj2YhKY7zZqCPMocObjufj2qNrkacgFEhazZ7n2iPdIIArMsE7Tnkm6Ws6AqUFcxgkC4B0sf7OkAmqA' alt='Ukraine&#x27;s President Volodymyr Zelensky reacts after receiving the International Four Freedoms Award in Middelburg, Netherlands, on April 16, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Loan terms: NDTV reported that the package would be funded through EU borrowing on capital markets and offered as interest-free loans for 2026 and 2027, backed by EU budget headroom.</li><li>Transit timing: Hungarian company MOL said Ukrtransnafta told it that crude began entering Ukraine from Belarus around noon on Wednesday, with first deliveries to Hungary and Slovakia expected by Thursday.</li><li>Supply dispute: Ukraine said the January halt followed war-related damage to the pipeline, while Moscow rejected that explanation and Hungary&#x27;s government accused Kyiv of deliberately blocking deliveries.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukraine: President Volodymyr Zelenskyy linked the completed pipeline repairs to progress on the EU support package and urged the bloc to unblock the funding once the infrastructure was restored. (<a href='https://apnews.com/article/ukraine-druzhba-pipeline-7dfc9574bf95a69eda13b1440171e402'>AP News</a>)</li><li>Hungary and Slovakia: Both countries made renewed oil access through Druzhba a condition for dropping their objections, and their operators said they expected supplies to resume immediately after Ukraine reopened transit. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/eu-loan-ukraine-aid-package-druzhba-hungary-slovakia/33737963.html'>RFE/RL</a>)</li><li>European Union: EU diplomats framed the approval as a step toward keeping Ukraine financially afloat over the next two years while also letting the bloc move ahead with another sanctions package on Russia. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/eu-unblocks-%E2%82%AC90-billion-loan-to-ukraine/a-76895753'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li><li>Slovakia: During the debate over the loan and pipeline, Prime Minister Robert Fico also criticized the incoming Hungarian government, in comments The Guardian said signaled possible strain in the previously close Slovak-Hungarian alignment on energy issues. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/22/ukraine-eu-90bn-loan-russia-war-hungary-zelenskyy-putin-magyar-orban-europe-latest-news-updates'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/22/2026/ukraine-reopens-russian-oil-pipeline-to-get-90b-eu-loan'>Ukraine reopens Russian oil pipeline to get €90B EU loan</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/638920-hungary-ukraine-druzhba-oil/'>Ukraine resumes oil flow via Druzhba pipeline – Hungary</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/22/ukraine-eu-90bn-loan-russia-war-hungary-zelenskyy-putin-magyar-orban-europe-latest-news-updates'>EU provisionally 